betterquesting.questline.D4B4PFfzWT2Q4DUgPjN9oQ.name=GregGuns
betterquesting.questline.D4B4PFfzWT2Q4DUgPjN9oQ.desc=Guns that follow GregTech progression.
betterquesting.quest.4XzaW-3VWNKZOIlttBqwpQ.name=Advanced Ammunition
betterquesting.quest.4XzaW-3VWNKZOIlttBqwpQ.desc=EV ammo: advanced magazines and minigun drums.
betterquesting.quest.vzLd-yXoXoqAjpPwKjGgFQ.name=Charging at the Right Tier
betterquesting.quest.vzLd-yXoXoqAjpPwKjGgFQ.desc=A GregGuns electric item has one tier. Only a charger or buffer of exactly that tier takes it.
betterquesting.quest.0I5k4WWbWyeGF7ZcFAjoiw.name=Ammo Depot
betterquesting.quest.0I5k4WWbWyeGF7ZcFAjoiw.desc=Stock 256 rounds in a chest: your own supply.
betterquesting.quest.k0l8Z9XGUd2iHk_8CCjnOA.name=Explosives Handling
betterquesting.quest.k0l8Z9XGUd2iHk_8CCjnOA.desc=Grenades and rockets need explosive dust. Store it away from the line.
betterquesting.quest.1fceSBv3UamtS9g-upePqA.name=Filling Bench (optional)
betterquesting.quest.1fceSBv3UamtS9g-upePqA.desc=An optional annex behind the packing end of the Works, built around six workbench tables. It loads magazines from the Works output.
betterquesting.quest.GvSjKY8wWcCuwQ_aNUAnQQ.name=Fuel Tanks
betterquesting.quest.GvSjKY8wWcCuwQ_aNUAnQQ.desc=Fuel tanks hold GT fuel. Diesel from the oil line works.
betterquesting.quest.Nw-e_L32UOm4-we1yYkBlw.name=Ammo Logistics
betterquesting.quest.Nw-e_L32UOm4-we1yYkBlw.desc=Ammo is the real cost of a gun. Build it as production, not as crafting.
betterquesting.quest.V7y4FFt1VQa-N8mwXKyomQ.name=Magazines in the Press
betterquesting.quest.V7y4FFt1VQa-N8mwXKyomQ.desc=The same press makes empty magazines and fills them, so one machine covers the whole chain.
betterquesting.quest.6-1J9c-KUrSOvgJ5NR2PkQ.name=Pipe It
betterquesting.quest.6-1J9c-KUrSOvgJ5NR2PkQ.desc=Move rounds and parts between machines with GT item pipes, so the line runs unattended.
betterquesting.quest.pijn8MOtV-ezyuZ1GzR0rg.name=Run the Press
betterquesting.quest.pijn8MOtV-ezyuZ1GzR0rg.desc=The Ammo Press makes rounds in bulk. Feed it GT parts and powder, and take the shells from its output.
betterquesting.quest.t09A1ZT-XI2ySLMI-VnX1Q.name=Ammunition Works
betterquesting.quest.t09A1ZT-XI2ySLMI-VnX1Q.desc=The Ammunition Works is a multiblock press hall with high parallels. Build it when one press cannot keep up. It needs an interior lamp.
betterquesting.quest.Ktu9FDk3W5-imEa0hwGXbQ.name=E. coli Culture
betterquesting.quest.Ktu9FDk3W5-imEa0hwGXbQ.desc=The Bio Gun runs on culture fluid. Brew Biomass, make the E. coli dish in the Bio Lab, then grow the culture in the BartWorks Bacterial Vat.
betterquesting.quest.uj_5v9mYVEeKzFmxhDVdnw.name=Bio Gun
betterquesting.quest.uj_5v9mYVEeKzFmxhDVdnw.desc=Sprays culture fluid that eats flesh. Refill it from the Bio Tank. The Nether Blaster later shares this chain.
betterquesting.quest.7V7dtADtUImcaUKp8HBOEQ.name=Bio Tank
betterquesting.quest.7V7dtADtUImcaUKp8HBOEQ.desc=The Bio Tank is built from a GT Large Fluid Cell. A Fluid Canner fills it with E. coli culture fluid.
betterquesting.quest.D110ToiWWbqWJnwAqvAPTw.name=Tesla or Sonic Rifle
betterquesting.quest.D110ToiWWbqWJnwAqvAPTw.desc=Specialist weapons. Pick one.
betterquesting.quest.knVvWsyhXNKqW5_Ifh1yBg.name=Energy Weapons
betterquesting.quest.knVvWsyhXNKqW5_Ifh1yBg.desc=EV adds lasers, pulse rifles and electric ammo. Titanium is the gate.
betterquesting.quest.tSdWXpg7WpWrfuyoRWiGOA.name=Laser Rifle
betterquesting.quest.tSdWXpg7WpWrfuyoRWiGOA.desc=Electric, so it charges at an EV battery buffer. An HV buffer will not accept it.
betterquesting.quest.anUXm2cHVEy3w23fQVfW_g.name=Laser Focus
betterquesting.quest.anUXm2cHVEy3w23fQVfW_g.desc=The Laser Focus is cut in a GT Laser Engraver at EV. It is the core of every laser weapon.
betterquesting.quest.18GPEk2JVFif2NroFsHLXw.name=Minigun
betterquesting.quest.18GPEk2JVFif2NroFsHLXw.desc=Drum-fed, very high fire rate. Heavy on ammo.
betterquesting.quest.MxpCG_RiXvGv_cMybdc68w.name=Pulse Rifle or PDW
betterquesting.quest.MxpCG_RiXvGv_cMybdc68w.desc=Advanced magazines are the EV ammo step up.
betterquesting.quest.ct79JLmwVza6IhVOWnSITg.name=Steam Armor
betterquesting.quest.ct79JLmwVza6IhVOWnSITg.desc=Bronze plate and cloth around a coal-fired chestplate. Burn Coal or Charcoal for speed and strength.
betterquesting.quest.Ijln77bBVEGQhTKU66-6Jg.name=Energy Weapons Done
betterquesting.quest.Ijln77bBVEGQhTKU66-6Jg.desc=IV brings blasters and power armor.
betterquesting.quest.sRKOlCwmVseOIo_9jtROkQ.name=T3 Combat Armor
betterquesting.quest.sRKOlCwmVseOIo_9jtROkQ.desc=Titanium plate in the EV Assembler.
betterquesting.quest.08Lhb4uVX4Clef_DTgvKLw.name=Gas Mask
betterquesting.quest.08Lhb4uVX4Clef_DTgvKLw.desc=A helmet-slot mask. GT hazards check armor slots only.
betterquesting.quest.OrL5XKPWWg6GJcQ_Lh3GEw.name=Glider
betterquesting.quest.OrL5XKPWWg6GJcQ_Lh3GEw.desc=Glide down from heights. Also in the wings slot.
betterquesting.quest.63bi8F0GU4qtylDedBiARA.name=Know Your Hazards
betterquesting.quest.63bi8F0GU4qtylDedBiARA.desc=Each protective item lists the hazards it blocks. Check the tooltip.
betterquesting.quest.sbT_rjFeWHivTHb6E8N5Pw.name=Equipment Slots
betterquesting.quest.sbT_rjFeWHivTHb6E8N5Pw.desc=Armor uses armor slots. Goggles, packs and pouches use Baubles slots.
betterquesting.quest.OeMwc2EdX3ybZ0eQTsRyKg.name=Jump Pack
betterquesting.quest.OeMwc2EdX3ybZ0eQTsRyKg.desc=Back device in the wings slot.
betterquesting.quest.hsYHfI3wU3GvcuCf2VyPQQ.name=Medkit
betterquesting.quest.hsYHfI3wU3GvcuCf2VyPQQ.desc=Heals you over time. Craft one before a fight.
betterquesting.quest.IDioba7CU1ORtYdr2qlldg.name=Night Vision Goggles
betterquesting.quest.IDioba7CU1ORtYdr2qlldg.desc=Wear in the head Baubles slot, not the helmet slot.
betterquesting.quest.X79n0oWKWuCqQYwCYI0VPw.name=Oxygen Mask and Tanks
betterquesting.quest.X79n0oWKWuCqQYwCYI0VPw.desc=For space and bad air. Needs compressed air.
betterquesting.quest.qT16OcFiXLahNbb0hFLu3A.name=Ammo Pouch
betterquesting.quest.qT16OcFiXLahNbb0hFLu3A.desc=Wear in the quiver Baubles slot.
betterquesting.quest.n0jkztrIW--cq29iq3tU0g.name=AS50
betterquesting.quest.n0jkztrIW--cq29iq3tU0g.desc=Anti-materiel rifle with its own magazines.
betterquesting.quest.YIoirIY4WpCQ1Ab-bNDp1w.name=Flamethrower
betterquesting.quest.YIoirIY4WpCQ1Ab-bNDp1w.desc=Burns GT fuel from a fuel tank. Diesel works.
betterquesting.quest.5lUh3JeXW82Mn5E5oL6xyA.name=Grenade Launcher
betterquesting.quest.5lUh3JeXW82Mn5E5oL6xyA.desc=Fires the 40 mm grenades you learned to make at MV.
betterquesting.quest.LJaUhufHUVSDgcoU_8jGcw.name=Heavy Arms
betterquesting.quest.LJaUhufHUVSDgcoU_8jGcw.desc=HV adds heavy weapons, launchers and electric tools. Stainless steel is the gate.
betterquesting.quest.jdNuu-ZwXCGTxyGIITt4oQ.name=LMG
betterquesting.quest.jdNuu-ZwXCGTxyGIITt4oQ.desc=Belt-fed and heavy. LMG magazines are an HV part.
betterquesting.quest._-zv3UWTW46bCXsTCjRQmA.name=AUG, SCAR or Vector
betterquesting.quest._-zv3UWTW46bCXsTCjRQmA.desc=Specialist rifles. Pick one; they are all HV builds.
betterquesting.quest.2xo9O6LeXQG5oYfZak5APA.name=Rocket Launcher
betterquesting.quest.2xo9O6LeXQG5oYfZak5APA.desc=Rockets need explosive dust and a circuit. Mind your own blast radius.
betterquesting.quest.bcXXo-9EW4ilXvMTgUopuA.name=Heavy Arms Done
betterquesting.quest.bcXXo-9EW4ilXvMTgUopuA.desc=EV brings energy weapons.
betterquesting.quest.IDtZWJGBXVmSPjlEoYvouA.name=Chainsaw and Power Hammer
betterquesting.quest.IDtZWJGBXVmSPjlEoYvouA.desc=Electric tools charge only in a charger or battery buffer of exactly their tier: HV.
betterquesting.quest.hw_7QfMgWvSvEBdcM5sh4g.name=Air-Defense Battery
betterquesting.quest.hw_7QfMgWvSvEBdcM5sh4g.desc=The battery holds 4 stacks of 16 SAMs and a Data Stick. Put a stick that carries a radar's link in its slot and it fires by itself at the nearest threat that radar reports, within 256 blocks: one SAM a second at most, 400 EU each. A SAM does 40 damage, so Tier 1 and Tier 2 missiles fall to one and a Tier 3 missile takes two. The warhead goes off where the missile is hit, so shoot early. Make a battery and a SAM.
betterquesting.quest.jnrSZsr_XfOI0sMCPeYxUQ.name=Automate the Body
betterquesting.quest.jnrSZsr_XfOI0sMCPeYxUQ.desc=Scan one hand-built body into a Data Stick in the Scanner, then the Assembly Line builds the basic body from plates, fins, an engine, 2 circuits (Advanced for Tier 1, Data for Tier 2) and 250 L of lubricant: 30 seconds for Tier 1, 45 for Tier 2. A better Guidance Computer is fitted afterwards in the Assembler: put the body and the computer in, and the same body comes out with that guidance.
betterquesting.quest.kbVxkPNqV8-lYmEtAdnFnQ.name=Missile Body
betterquesting.quest.kbVxkPNqV8-lYmEtAdnFnQ.desc=On the NASA Workbench page, build a Missile Body T1: three compressed steel plates in one column, four Galacticraft Tier 1 rocket fins, a Galacticraft Tier 1 engine and a Guidance Computer Mk I. Compressed plates come from the Implosion Compressor. There is no warhead slot; the warhead goes on at the pad. A better Guidance Computer makes the missile land closer.
betterquesting.quest.4KjNfDUmXW28JarHt0SHGA.name=Missile Chip
betterquesting.quest.4KjNfDUmXW28JarHt0SHGA.desc=Every missile starts as a chip. The GregTech Circuit Assembler makes a Missile Chip T1 at HV from an Advanced Plastic Circuit Board, 2 Advanced circuits and 4 fine gold wire. The Tier 2 chip is made at EV from an Advanced Epoxy Circuit Board, 2 Data circuits and 4 fine electrum wire. Make a Tier 1 chip.
betterquesting.quest.I9JCb4IjWZ-4KPHIS_CDlA.name=Launch Control
betterquesting.quest.I9JCb4IjWZ-4KPHIS_CDlA.desc=Place a Launch Control block within 4 blocks of the pad and power it at HV. Type the target X and Z, or load them from a Data Stick. The screen shows the range (at least 20 blocks, at most 1,000 for Tier 1) and the blast radius to expect.
betterquesting.quest.rQaB9lE6UTKiPd5-PZNH4Q.name=Demolition Charge
betterquesting.quest.rQaB9lE6UTKiPd5-PZNH4Q.desc=Place a warhead where you want the hole and light it with Flint and Steel, a Fire Charge or a redstone pulse. The fuse is 3 seconds plus 1 second per 3 blocks of blast radius, so a full Condensed warhead gives you 6. Get well clear, and keep other charges away: another explosion sets one off in half a second.
betterquesting.quest.4iGni58RWjWEJwmVI20ehw.name=EMP Tower
betterquesting.quest.4iGni58RWjWEJwmVI20ehw.desc=The EMP Tower sends one pulse when you press Fire, on a redstone rising edge or from a computer. The radius is yours, 4 to 100 blocks, and the pulse costs 25 EU per square block of radius: 90,000 EU at 60. It drains the 64 nearest machines, batteries and Battery Buffers to zero and gives each multiblock one maintenance issue. A missile in range is destroyed 50 percent of the time, has its guidance fried 40 percent and has its warhead set off 1 percent. Build one, and keep it away from your own base.
betterquesting.quest.jCjcKUqDWJezjQmc98WtTw.name=Fuel the Missile
betterquesting.quest.jCjcKUqDWJezjQmc98WtTw.desc=Attach a Galacticraft Fuel Loader to the pad. A Tier 1 missile takes 2,000 mB of RP-1 or Cetane-Boosted Diesel, or better. Fuel left unburned at impact makes the blast up to 25 percent bigger, so a closer target hits harder.
betterquesting.quest.TB8tfZEMWJ67-7Wz1ovSCA.name=Handheld Tools
betterquesting.quest.TB8tfZEMWJ67-7Wz1ovSCA.desc=The Radar Gun aims 200 blocks and stores that spot as a target; right-click a Launch Control to copy it. The Remote Detonator links to a placed warhead when you sneak-click it, and a right-click lights its fuse from 128 blocks (HV), 256 (EV) or 512 (IV). The Defuser puts a lit fuse out, or takes a missile on its pad apart before the engines light; it lasts 32 uses. Make all three.
betterquesting.quest.Y2gOH5_qWrOdflkhB64vCg.name=First Launch
betterquesting.quest.Y2gOH5_qWrOdflkhB64vCg.desc=Press Launch, or send the block a redstone pulse. After two seconds of warm-up the missile climbs, flies its arc and detonates on impact; a Tier 1 flight at full range takes about a minute. The pad, the fuel loader and the Launch Control come through unharmed. Make sure nobody stands at the target.
betterquesting.quest.oXlfsvjaVNmda25AXg-SwQ.name=Nuclear Warhead
betterquesting.quest.oXlfsvjaVNmda25AXg-SwQ.desc=The nuclear warhead is a Tier 3 casing at ZPM, two blocks tall, made in the Assembler from tungstensteel plates, Industrial TNT, Plastic Explosive, uranium-235, plutonium and a Fuze Assembly Mk III. It flies only on a Tier 3 missile from the silo. A full warhead blasts 64 blocks, and nothing living inside the inner 60 percent (38 blocks at full fill) survives, bosses included. The top layer of ground is left irradiated for about an hour: cross it in full hazmat armor. Launch one from your silo, and stand well back.
betterquesting.quest.4TbIziOkWxSMv8pMnJE2dA.name=Stack It on the Pad
betterquesting.quest.4TbIziOkWxSMv8pMnJE2dA.desc=Place the Missile Body on the middle of a Galacticraft Launch Pad, then set a warhead on its nose; it seats flush. Sneak and right-click the body with an empty hand to arm it, which turns the stack into a missile.
betterquesting.quest.70Tzn2miVgKdpAJQSq449g.name=Radar
betterquesting.quest.70Tzn2miVgKdpAJQSq449g.desc=A radar watches the missiles in flight and flags the ones that will land inside its protected radius, which you set on its screen (64 blocks to begin with). The HV radar sees 128 blocks and the EV radar 256, flat, at any height. A missile that only passes over is tracked but not a threat. The redstone it puts out on every side is the number of incoming missiles, up to 15. Right-click it with a Data Stick to save its link for a battery. Build a radar and power it.
betterquesting.quest.Xmv-nEDuUGOM661dF3bKgg.name=Radar Tower
betterquesting.quest.Xmv-nEDuUGOM661dF3bKgg.desc=The Radar Tower is a 3 by 3 tower of Radar Casing, 7 blocks tall, with a Gantry Beam mast up the middle. Make the casing four at a time in the Assembler at IV from 6 tungsten steel plates. Its range comes from its weakest Energy Hatch: 512 blocks at IV, 768 at LuV, 1,024 at ZPM, 1,280 at UV and 1,536 at UHV. Put an Energy Hatch and a Maintenance Hatch in the bottom ring, and set the protected radius from the R button on the controller screen. Build the controller.
betterquesting.quest.ctrVSbsBX6KoGm8-pujtow.name=Engrave the Schematic
betterquesting.quest.ctrVSbsBX6KoGm8-pujtow.desc=Put the chip and a Red lens (Tier 2: Blue) in the Laser Engraver. The lens is not used up. Slot the finished Missile Schematic into the Galacticraft NASA Workbench to open the missile's page.
betterquesting.quest.FKODJ5uAW3m6h_n9FGLxtA.name=Missile Silo
betterquesting.quest.FKODJ5uAW3m6h_n9FGLxtA.desc=Missiles launch from the Missile Silo, a 5 by 5 tower you build from Light or Dark Concrete (any finish but cobblestone) and clear glass (Tinkers' Construct or EnderIO) around an open 3 by 3 shaft, with a Galacticraft Launch Pad for its floor and a ring of Gantry Beams on top. The controller is an HV machine, and the Energy Hatch sets what it launches: HV for Tier 1, EV for Tier 2, LuV for Tier 3. A silo shot flies 25%% farther and scatters half as much. Fit an Input Bus for bodies and warheads, an Input Hatch for fuel, an Energy Hatch and a Maintenance Hatch in place of any wall, glass or floor-ring block, but not the rim or the pad. Feed it a body and a warhead and it stands the missile in the shaft for you. Build the silo and put a Launch Control within 6 blocks of it.
betterquesting.quest.Hpt25drUVxG-X28laN9_ng.name=Titanium Casing
betterquesting.quest.Hpt25drUVxG-X28laN9_ng.desc=The Tier 2 casing is made of titanium and holds up to 20 charges, four times the 5 charges of the Tier 1 casing. Its blast types are made in the Assembler at EV, from eight titanium plates, Industrial TNT, Plastic Explosive and a Fuze Assembly Mk II. Make a Tier 2 warhead.
betterquesting.quest.LuSV9ZftUmKkTqpC2lzM8g.name=Tier 2 Missile
betterquesting.quest.LuSV9ZftUmKkTqpC2lzM8g.desc=Tier 2 flies up to 3,000 blocks and carries a titanium-cased warhead. Its chip is made at EV, its body takes six titanium plates, and it burns 4,000 mB of Dense Hydrazine or better. Build it, fuel it and launch it.
betterquesting.quest.jt554mmwW4GO64BnyW_bUw.name=Your First Warhead
betterquesting.quest.jt554mmwW4GO64BnyW_bUw.desc=A warhead is a GregTech-built charge: a stainless steel casing around TNT and a payload. The starter recipe in the Assembler makes a Condensed warhead with a fill of 1 from 2 stainless steel plates, 2 TNT and a Fuze Assembly Mk I. Make one and keep it.
betterquesting.quest.NptPg74nWFqUKvO9--I43g.name=Anti-Gravity Device
betterquesting.quest.NptPg74nWFqUKvO9--I43g.desc=Back device for flight. Needs the wings slot.
betterquesting.quest.5_c7J85gU2aixhHqkqv1BQ.name=Blaster Rifle
betterquesting.quest.5_c7J85gU2aixhHqkqv1BQ.desc=High-damage energy rifle at IV voltage.
betterquesting.quest.x2lMGKJZWK2Xms6e1LPpgw.name=De-Atomizer Pistol
betterquesting.quest.x2lMGKJZWK2Xms6e1LPpgw.desc=One pistol or two; the akimbo pair needs the offhand slot.
betterquesting.quest.lH0-MO5VUxWBnzwgiVP8Cw.name=Exo Suit
betterquesting.quest.lH0-MO5VUxWBnzwgiVP8Cw.desc=Strength and carry bonuses.
betterquesting.quest.d1LoNVF1UVesinyYYLwYUQ.name=Golden Revolver
betterquesting.quest.d1LoNVF1UVesinyYYLwYUQ.desc=A showpiece sidearm. Single or akimbo.
betterquesting.quest.yW5t2nDLXIaIW8EBTAoYYw.name=Power Armor Era
betterquesting.quest.yW5t2nDLXIaIW8EBTAoYYw.desc=IV adds blasters, power armor and the anti-grav device. Tungstensteel is the gate.
betterquesting.quest.G3OzWb1tU8i_ycAZ3Q7TMQ.name=Power Armor
betterquesting.quest.G3OzWb1tU8i_ycAZ3Q7TMQ.desc=Full powered suit. Charge it at an IV buffer.
betterquesting.quest.Bd2n0deSWSu_UTiW5dRIcg.name=Scatter Laser Rifle
betterquesting.quest.Bd2n0deSWSu_UTiW5dRIcg.desc=A shotgun-style laser. Short range, wide spread.
betterquesting.quest.XgnwF9KwUOSKhZqv58tAcQ.name=Power Armor Era Done
betterquesting.quest.XgnwF9KwUOSKhZqv58tAcQ.desc=LuV recipes use the Assembly Line.
betterquesting.quest.weAPoFjqUAqgN3uN-vZULg.name=Alien Blaster
betterquesting.quest.weAPoFjqUAqgN3uN-vZULg.desc=LuV energy weapon.
betterquesting.quest._hpgISrBUFq7uIkJaGtsdw.name=Grim Reaper
betterquesting.quest._hpgISrBUFq7uIkJaGtsdw.desc=Late-game close-range weapon.
betterquesting.quest.ktnOv_R0XRCvYYG60Dpfmg.name=Assembly-Line Weapons
betterquesting.quest.ktnOv_R0XRCvYYG60Dpfmg.desc=LuV weapons are built in the Assembly Line with a research item, like GT's own LuV parts.
betterquesting.quest.SeBngdKKUsysDcTsJvjiqA.name=Nether Blaster
betterquesting.quest.SeBngdKKUsysDcTsJvjiqA.desc=Fires nether charges. Mind the splash.
betterquesting.quest.ID9t77f7UgaJ8R1kiS9a8A.name=Nether Charge
betterquesting.quest.ID9t77f7UgaJ8R1kiS9a8A.desc=The explosive behind the Nether Blaster.
betterquesting.quest.LxA9nvbuWduXmAVgymB0Sg.name=LuV Arms Done
betterquesting.quest.LxA9nvbuWduXmAVgymB0Sg.desc=ZPM is the top of the GregGuns tree.
betterquesting.quest.Mz-uO4DjXsKUCga3SdfpiQ.name=9mm Rounds
betterquesting.quest.Mz-uO4DjXsKUCga3SdfpiQ.desc=The Ammo Press builds 9mm rounds from a GT round, a foil casing and gunpowder. Check the Ammo Press tab in NEI.
betterquesting.quest.uDmM8VcaUEejFs-ZPe9QRQ.name=Ammo Press
betterquesting.quest.uDmM8VcaUEejFs-ZPe9QRQ.desc=Ammo is made in the GregGuns Ammo Press, not in a GT Assembler. Build the LV press: it has its own recipe list in NEI.
betterquesting.quest.XzCp7O1kWYW7UEyUcRinjQ.name=Bolt Action Rifle
betterquesting.quest.XzCp7O1kWYW7UEyUcRinjQ.desc=Long range and slow to cycle. Right-click to zoom.
betterquesting.quest.apiZbYKfWCSb47TsYpHd0Q.name=T1 Combat Armor
betterquesting.quest.apiZbYKfWCSb47TsYpHd0Q.desc=Steel plate pressed in the LV Assembler.
betterquesting.quest.hYUeOT7cXjOoCT5LMikuZA.name=Steel-Age Firearms
betterquesting.quest.hYUeOT7cXjOoCT5LMikuZA.desc=LV opens steel guns. The last step of each recipe is an LV machine.
betterquesting.quest.boi3n217UI6XIPY0yyxEVQ.name=Magazines
betterquesting.quest.boi3n217UI6XIPY0yyxEVQ.desc=Empty and filled magazines are Ammo Press recipes too. Sneak-click a magazine to empty it.
betterquesting.quest.chM3O2OvW4ilHfb1FAhltA.name=Knife or Crowbar
betterquesting.quest.chM3O2OvW4ilHfb1FAhltA.desc=Melee tools never run dry.
betterquesting.quest.mJR67SnRUAyj7d-tQP9low.name=9mm Pistol
betterquesting.quest.mJR67SnRUAyj7d-tQP9low.desc=Your first real sidearm. Magazine-fed.
betterquesting.quest.NsiOegLwXQeQiJScpSPrjA.name=Revolver
betterquesting.quest.NsiOegLwXQeQiJScpSPrjA.desc=A heavier sidearm. Compare its damage with the pistol on the tooltip.
betterquesting.quest.PUU_uhcLWImmqnZiZfJu-g.name=Sawed Off
betterquesting.quest.PUU_uhcLWImmqnZiZfJu-g.desc=Spread pellets: strong at point-blank range, weak far away. Uses shotgun shells.
betterquesting.quest.q59wXd1mV1WcX1YeUf6dfA.name=Steel Age Done
betterquesting.quest.q59wXd1mV1WcX1YeUf6dfA.desc=MV needs aluminum and a bigger power setup. Move on when your GT line gets there.
betterquesting.quest.QuPctiU0UTysPZKi-tEFjA.name=Armory Gantry
betterquesting.quest.QuPctiU0UTysPZKi-tEFjA.desc=The Gantry is a multiblock repair hall with a row of bays, for armor and guns in bulk. Its controller is HV and it needs an interior lamp.
betterquesting.quest.wiZf_nJjUDWSzPXMNLmtlw.name=GregGuns Machines
betterquesting.quest.wiZf_nJjUDWSzPXMNLmtlw.desc=Most machines are plain GT. Only the Repair Bench and the Turret are GregGuns' own.
betterquesting.quest.HJVu3hFmXUeXp1q2JY1lcA.name=Mending a Weapon
betterquesting.quest.HJVu3hFmXUeXp1q2JY1lcA.desc=Put a damaged gun and its gate material in the bench.
betterquesting.quest.z8faDvh0UvemqxE8s6CRxQ.name=Repair Bench
betterquesting.quest.z8faDvh0UvemqxE8s6CRxQ.desc=Mends guns and armor using the item's gate material. Tier is provisional (MV) until area 09 settles it.
betterquesting.quest.F4G1fstlX7WJJh6m9opOfA.name=Turret
betterquesting.quest.F4G1fstlX7WJJh6m9opOfA.desc=Automatic defense. Tier is provisional (HV) until area 09 settles it.
betterquesting.quest.XCqKCGtOU02fIt4JMyjTzw.name=Powering the Turret
betterquesting.quest.XCqKCGtOU02fIt4JMyjTzw.desc=The turret takes EU at its tier. Overvoltage damages it.
betterquesting.quest.qz639_9iXPChHoN46iJdPQ.name=Friend or Foe
betterquesting.quest.qz639_9iXPChHoN46iJdPQ.desc=Turrets spare you and your allies on a GTNHLib team, and shoot hostiles.
betterquesting.quest.yOzpMokqUwe66PdRL7Lcyg.name=Akimbo
betterquesting.quest.yOzpMokqUwe66PdRL7Lcyg.desc=A matching pistol in each hand. Needs the offhand slot.
betterquesting.quest.lypD0jUiVxK_GAPc5kkxMw.name=Combat Shotgun
betterquesting.quest.lypD0jUiVxK_GAPc5kkxMw.desc=Magazine-fed shotgun. Uses the same shells as the Sawed Off.
betterquesting.quest.CxLbdj1wXiCSjt4IO5DHvA.name=Flashbang
betterquesting.quest.CxLbdj1wXiCSjt4IO5DHvA.desc=Blinds and stuns instead of killing. Useful for clearing a camp.
betterquesting.quest.SkjH3vntWvqub9jvearFeg.name=Frag Grenade
betterquesting.quest.SkjH3vntWvqub9jvearFeg.desc=Explosives need TNT dust from the GT line. Throw from a safe distance.
betterquesting.quest.liaFkCI8Wret4DrZAA9GQw.name=Aluminum-Age Arms
betterquesting.quest.liaFkCI8Wret4DrZAA9GQw.desc=MV adds automatic weapons, grenades and second-tier armor. Aluminum is the gate.
betterquesting.quest.gPKVACp0U7-bbCtwGWRsHQ.name=M4 or AK47
betterquesting.quest.gPKVACp0U7-bbCtwGWRsHQ.desc=Assault rifles use their own magazines, not SMG magazines.
betterquesting.quest.P59k8AiKWgmAaH75tkGLXg.name=SMG Magazines
betterquesting.quest.P59k8AiKWgmAaH75tkGLXg.desc=Press an empty magazine in the Ammo Press, then fill it with rounds.
betterquesting.quest.F6wvUKf0XpmlAqliuUYTtw.name=Aluminum Age Done
betterquesting.quest.F6wvUKf0XpmlAqliuUYTtw.desc=HV brings heavy weapons and stainless steel.
betterquesting.quest.eWJcwTF7Uqq5lbmE95P4Fg.name=T2 Armor
betterquesting.quest.eWJcwTF7Uqq5lbmE95P4Fg.desc=Combat, Commando or Riot. Pick the set that suits your style.
betterquesting.quest.ylGIBgZrXvKLESd_27N5MA.name=Thompson SMG
betterquesting.quest.ylGIBgZrXvKLESd_27N5MA.desc=Fast, light automatic fire at MV.
betterquesting.quest.lYUjVBo5WV29u03j0mJOMw.name=Alien Bug
betterquesting.quest.lYUjVBo5WV29u03j0mJOMw.desc=A config-gated boss from the bug nest.
betterquesting.quest.syP7nK4rUwirzv6x-PBQcA.name=Army Soldiers
betterquesting.quest.syP7nK4rUwirzv6x-PBQcA.desc=Disciplined and well armed. They carry MV ammunition.
betterquesting.quest.kYI6SLykVpiRBdyquFfUMA.name=Bandits and Outcasts
betterquesting.quest.kYI6SLykVpiRBdyquFfUMA.desc=Raiders carry LV gear. Expect 9mm drops.
betterquesting.quest.4gg1AG4HXMadTcKsWXWc8w.name=Commandos and Stormtroopers
betterquesting.quest.4gg1AG4HXMadTcKsWXWc8w.desc=Elite soldiers. Armor up first.
betterquesting.quest.KX-pQPLZWgSCTyjXwnLAJg.name=Cyberdemon
betterquesting.quest.KX-pQPLZWgSCTyjXwnLAJg.desc=A config-gated late boss. No natural spawn.
betterquesting.quest.R02XjcLfWyuLzIo6xjcahQ.name=Dictator Dave
betterquesting.quest.R02XjcLfWyuLzIo6xjcahQ.desc=A secret mini-boss with a Golden Revolver. Appears only from spawn eggs or the pack's own spawner setup.
betterquesting.quest.Gr5HlmnTVcKuwMy565oUBA.name=Elite Variants
betterquesting.quest.Gr5HlmnTVcKuwMy565oUBA.desc=Kill one elite Infernal mob: up to five modifiers, glowing name. Tick the box when you have.
betterquesting.quest.P0cM5jjnWWi0jPfg1nfTaw.name=Attack Helicopter
betterquesting.quest.P0cM5jjnWWi0jPfg1nfTaw.desc=A flying boss with its own health bar. Bring launchers.
betterquesting.quest.t8BhfdgpVnCMaZTth-goMQ.name=Infernal Variants
betterquesting.quest.t8BhfdgpVnCMaZTth-goMQ.desc=Kill one infernal-rank mob. It can drop rare HV items.
betterquesting.quest.a315yLzbWASFSYtqJlkyDQ.name=Hostile Factions
betterquesting.quest.a315yLzbWASFSYtqJlkyDQ.desc=Soldiers, bandits and zombies roam the Overworld. Some carry guns; some drop ammo.
betterquesting.quest.YGbgOq4_WZWQaK62pgw0zw.name=Skeleton Soldiers
betterquesting.quest.YGbgOq4_WZWQaK62pgw0zw.desc=Armed skeletons shoot back. Use cover.
betterquesting.quest.80v0VhPfVBKUVzQY1NhNKQ.name=Psycho Steve
betterquesting.quest.80v0VhPfVBKUVzQY1NhNKQ.desc=A chainsaw mini-boss. His drop is tier-legal for the Overworld, not an HV saw.
betterquesting.quest.WzjEdlpfX7CnoQWAB1Vjeg.name=Ultra Variants
betterquesting.quest.WzjEdlpfX7CnoQWAB1Vjeg.desc=Kill one ultra Infernal mob. Ultra drops are MV.
betterquesting.quest.HNX5vy9IXyWXlDl05MGb6w.name=Walking Dead
betterquesting.quest.HNX5vy9IXyWXlDl05MGb6w.desc=Hunt the zombie variants: soldiers, farmers and miners.
betterquesting.quest.Tkq4h6W7X9WBrKfavb-TUQ.name=Big Bunker
betterquesting.quest.Tkq4h6W7X9WBrKfavb-TUQ.desc=Reinforced chests and soldiers. MV ceiling.
betterquesting.quest.OKZ9OGCiXDOv_DYYvjYKlA.name=Military Camp
betterquesting.quest.OKZ9OGCiXDOv_DYYvjYKlA.desc=Tents, barracks and a flag. Many soldiers.
betterquesting.quest.l1PRgHu1Vley1Cdb74iqiA.name=Dungeon Weapons
betterquesting.quest.l1PRgHu1Vley1Cdb74iqiA.desc=Roguelike dungeons drop weapons by depth: LV near the surface, MV deeper.
betterquesting.quest.hT8IW5j8U86nS3mZn_bUiw.name=Ruins and Camps
betterquesting.quest.hT8IW5j8U86nS3mZn_bUiw.desc=Natural structures dot the Overworld: factories, houses, bunkers, camps and ships. Their chests hold tiered gear.
betterquesting.quest._UPNUiNWV1O-jO_H9CIL7Q.name=Carrier and Submarine
betterquesting.quest._UPNUiNWV1O-jO_H9CIL7Q.desc=Large structures with MV weapon chests.
betterquesting.quest.sv2TkVqVX8a9uLShdPxeiw.name=Small Ruins
betterquesting.quest.sv2TkVqVX8a9uLShdPxeiw.desc=Factory building, train station, medium house and gas station. Their chests hold LV gear.
betterquesting.quest.B5FdBkr1X5auKNEWfCQlrw.name=Trigger: EV Tier Skip
betterquesting.quest.B5FdBkr1X5auKNEWfCQlrw.desc=No Description
betterquesting.quest._5Sldx3_Ub2sSg-JopCQFA.name=Trigger: HV Tier Skip
betterquesting.quest._5Sldx3_Ub2sSg-JopCQFA.desc=No Description
betterquesting.quest.k7wUDquJVQmraumbOZepmA.name=Trigger: IV Tier Skip
betterquesting.quest.k7wUDquJVQmraumbOZepmA.desc=No Description
betterquesting.quest.AWPf1dBEWb-1f6Fu0hDXKA.name=Trigger: LuV Tier Skip
betterquesting.quest.AWPf1dBEWb-1f6Fu0hDXKA.desc=No Description
betterquesting.quest.uHCMvP2aV_m0RNlKG4Jj2Q.name=Trigger: LV Tier Skip
betterquesting.quest.uHCMvP2aV_m0RNlKG4Jj2Q.desc=No Description
betterquesting.quest.GDgXwpofX9WTCxrBYRc88Q.name=Trigger: MV Tier Skip
betterquesting.quest.GDgXwpofX9WTCxrBYRc88Q.desc=No Description
betterquesting.quest.HDvCr0RvVvu2QvKev1mvOg.name=Trigger: ZPM Tier Skip
betterquesting.quest.HDvCr0RvVvu2QvKev1mvOg.desc=No Description
betterquesting.quest.6WgUfKHLVritlMHwZhD7tA.name=Ammo and Magazines
betterquesting.quest.6WgUfKHLVritlMHwZhD7tA.desc=Each gun takes one caliber. Loose rounds fill a magazine; sneak-click a magazine to empty it.
betterquesting.quest.edcduXKkVtWx2j1rZqdF-w.name=Fire, Reload, Zoom
betterquesting.quest.edcduXKkVtWx2j1rZqdF-w.desc=Hold use to fire, press the reload key to swap magazines, right-click to zoom. Rebind keys in Controls.
betterquesting.quest.ys8eY6RtV8iTwNNw6IVUOA.name=Where Gear Comes From
betterquesting.quest.ys8eY6RtV8iTwNNw6IVUOA.desc=Craft it in GT machines, or find it: quest loot bags, chests in ruins, drops from hostile soldiers. NEI lists every recipe and drop.
betterquesting.quest.W8qR4fyDX_aDk-g-tcevbw.name=Reading a Tier
betterquesting.quest.W8qR4fyDX_aDk-g-tcevbw.desc=An LV item needs an LV machine and steel, an MV item needs aluminum, and so on. Tooltips show the tier.
betterquesting.quest.NW0ZimUpUzOLzQ6eAO4Nvg.name=Welcome to GregGuns
betterquesting.quest.NW0ZimUpUzOLzQ6eAO4Nvg.desc=Guns here follow GregTech progression: each weapon needs a machine tier and a gate material. This tab walks you up the tiers.
betterquesting.quest.97ByAsUoUs6TYUKXeYpGHw.name=First Blood
betterquesting.quest.97ByAsUoUs6TYUKXeYpGHw.desc=Shoot five zombies with the Hand Cannon. Reload between shots.
betterquesting.quest.eQ7hWE3jV5y_EliMziLpsw.name=Hand Cannon
betterquesting.quest.eQ7hWE3jV5y_EliMziLpsw.desc=A single-shot bronze and wrought-iron cannon. Slow and loud.
betterquesting.quest.Id6LqXtlVYKNNi_Lh3NZuQ.name=Steam-Age Arms
betterquesting.quest.Id6LqXtlVYKNNi_Lh3NZuQ.desc=Bronze and wrought iron are enough for a first firearm. No electricity needed.
betterquesting.quest.TCrRly4gVIaC56th9bwd2w.name=T1 Miner Armor
betterquesting.quest.TCrRly4gVIaC56th9bwd2w.desc=Miner set, crafted from bronze plate and wrought iron.
